WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:07.309
Roles and workflows define how your organization works: who may do which step, and the steps a card goes through.

2
00:00:08.018 --> 00:00:14.390
Open Roles and workflows in the sidebar. The Roles tab lists your custom roles and the built-in ones.

3
00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:23.854
Built-in roles ship with the app. You can extend them with extra instructions, skills and standing orders, but their core rules stay.

4
00:00:24.556 --> 00:00:32.321
The Workflows tab lists every workflow with its versions. View shows the Code workflow as a diagram, step by step.

5
00:00:33.021 --> 00:00:36.864
Compare with previous lists what changed from the version before.

6
00:00:37.566 --> 00:00:43.497
A custom workflow is edited in the builder. New version opens it on a copy of the current one.

7
00:00:44.195 --> 00:00:54.271
Add a step, name it, and choose who does it. Save draft keeps it as a draft; nothing changes until you send it for approval and approve it on the desk.

8
00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:59.150
Back in the list, the new draft compares against the active version.

9
00:00:59.852 --> 00:01:06.549
A department groups the roles and workflows of one function. Type a name and choose Create department.

10
00:01:07.253 --> 00:01:16.063
In Design with the BA, start a design chat and describe the role or workflow you need. The BA drafts it and puts it on your desk for approval.

11
00:01:16.763 --> 00:01:22.301
That is Roles and workflows: shape how your team works, one approved version at a time.
